From 2318f189380e8915bc77c1e020392f773b2731ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lev Kozlov <kozlov.l.a10@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:17:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat: variable_max_stiffness.rotational may go to 1000 Nm/rad
 (was 100)

The ceiling clamps task.k_rot_*, whose own bound is 5000. At 100 on the KUKA iiwa14 with the
UMI, rotation trails its target by ~200 ms (pixi_kuka_ros2 track_tune sweeps 2-3, 26 Sep 2026:
lag ~= (d_rot + ~11 hidden) / k_rot), and no damping choice gets under that.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PYsbnsZbpqrrGZhLJYaMks
---
 src/cartesian_controller.yaml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/cartesian_controller.yaml b/src/cartesian_controller.yaml
index 01a17c8..1b4c5c6 100644
--- a/src/cartesian_controller.yaml
+++ b/src/cartesian_controller.yaml
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@ cartesian_controller:
       default_value: 60.0
       description: "Maximum allowed rotational stiffness value. Stiffness values above this will be clamped."
       validation:
-        bounds<>: [0.0, 100.0]
+        bounds<>: [0.0, 1000.0]
 
   variable_stiffness:
     enabled:
-- 
